Z||000000||Urchin||09-12-2001||09:18 PM||||Anyone know what this "black box" they keep reffering to is?  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/final.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||09-12-2001||09:21 PM||||Its a flight data recorder.  It records everything the plane does, acceleration, change of course, altitude, location etc. etc.  Everything.  Even the conversations between the pilots/ATC.<P>They will find them eventually.  No matter how bad the crash is. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Urchin||09-12-2001||09:22 PM||||That makes sense.... thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||09-12-2001||09:25 PM||||Commercial aircraft have a flight recorder that records the position of controls, engine speed, etc. during the entire flight. Varying amounts of info depending on the aircraft but most have enough info to re-create what happened during the flight. Most also have a cockpit voice recorder that records conversations in the cockpit. These are in VERY durable containers that will survive most crashes. I doubt they survived the WTC or Pentagon crashes though...||||reg||1
